Subject: [PATCH] tcp: a spawned endpoint is not bound until BindChild() binds it

spawn_pending_socket() copies the listening socket's local address into
the new socket, so a fresh child endpoint already looks bound
(IsBound() is true for 0.0.0.0:22), although only BindChild() puts it
into the endpoint hash. When _Spawn() failed before that - in particular
when BindChild() itself failed because the SYN's destination was no
longer a local address while the interfaces were going down at shutdown
- the child stayed among the listener's pending children, and when the
listener was freed, ~TCPEndpoint() -> Unbind() panicked:

  PANIC: bound endpoint 0xffffffff89de3c00 not in hash!
  Thread 142 "sshd"
    EndpointManager::Unbind
    TCPEndpoint::~TCPEndpoint
    tcp_uninit_protocol
    put_domain_protocols
    net_socket_private::~net_socket_private   (the child)
    net_socket_private::~net_socket_private   (the listener)
    socket_free

On an x86_64 VM this hit 8 of 13 reboots while an ssh client kept trying
to connect during shutdown. _Spawn() now clears the inherited address
first, the way Unbind() does, so the child is bound exactly when it is
in the hash.

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
index 52bb0b5289..cfd1ac7a51 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
@@ -1562,6 +1562,13 @@ TCPEndpoint::_Spawn(TCPEndpoint* parent, tcp_segment_header& segment,
 
 	TRACE("Spawn()");
 
+	// spawn_pending_socket() copied the listening socket's local address
+	// into ours, so we look bound, but only BindChild() puts us into the
+	// endpoint hash. If we fail before that (the destination is no longer
+	// a local address while the interfaces go down, for one), the
+	// destructor's Unbind() panicked with "bound endpoint not in hash".
+	(*LocalAddress())->sa_len = 0;
+
 	// TODO: proper error handling!
 	if (ProtocolSocket::Open() != B_OK) {
 		T(Error(this, "opening failed", __LINE__));
